From 76535c88f10ca13707a95138aee64693cab21b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zebulan Stanphill <zebulanstanphill@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:14:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UWP: Build Ring Racers as a static library for the UWP
 launcher

Adds SRB2_CONFIG_UWP (and the ninja-x64_windows_uwp_vcpkg-release preset),
which builds the game as a static library to be linked into the UWP
launcher from ringracers-uwp. Based on worleydl's uwp-compat branch of
RingRacers-dev, rebased onto v2.4.

- Pull the SDL2 headers and libuwp from worleydl/uwp-dep instead of vcpkg
- Render through OpenGL ES 2 (ANGLE on Direct3D 11): support OpenGL ES 2
  contexts in the GL2 RHI backend, request one, render at the size of
  ANGLE's surface, and hide Legacy GL, which needs desktop OpenGL
- Read game data and save files from E:\ringracers
- Use the libuwp display size and refresh rate instead of SDL's
- Force WASAPI audio
- Write the log to E:\ringracers\latest-log.txt, since the working
  directory is the read-only package folder
- Create the save folder before checking that the config is writable
- Log the OpenGL strings, surface size, shader compiles, and each step
  of the first frames, to diagnose startup on Xbox
- Skip the DbgHelp minidump handler and cpptrace, which can't work from
  the app container
- Show only the error in the crash dialog, which the Xbox cuts off,
  followed by which drives the app can see and whether each has a
  ringracers folder, and save it to E:\ringracers\error.txt
